  data: {
    LLM: "For Beginners:\n1. Learn the 16 point cards (A, K, Q, J of each suit)\n2. If you're kankei, coordinate with your partner through the card exchange\n3. Save the joker for critical tricks (but must play it in 9th trick)\n4. Count points taken to know if you're on track\n\n1. Track which point cards have been played\n2. As mukankei, cooperate with other non-partners to stop kankei\n3. Use the seat exchange rule to your advantage\n4. Calculate whether kankei can reach 9+ points based on visible cards\n\n1. Complex probability of joker location based on bidding\n2. Optimal card exchange strategies for partners\n3. Bluffing by bidding behavior\n4. Endgame calculation for exact point distribution\n5. Tournament scoring optimization over multiple rounds",
